= Acknowledgements

Pursuing a PhD is choosing to embark on an adventure filled with uncertainties and unexpected turns.
The investment is considerable, but the journey and its rewards are just as significant.
Despite its solitary nature, one should not underestimate the number and importance of the people who support the candidate along the way.
I was truly fortunate to be surrounded by remarkable individuals who were instrumental throughout this journey.

I want to start by deeply thanking my three supervisors, Xavier-Alameda Pineda, Laurent Girin and Chris Reinke.
They offered me their trust from the very beginning by selecting me among many competitive applicants, and they accompanied me with unfaltering support until the very end.
My PhD certainly did not spare us scientific difficulties, complications, or setbacks, yet they always managed to keep the hope and vision alive when I sometimes felt like losing confidence.
Their complementary expertise, their patience, and their kindness made every discussion immensely valuable.
The hours we spent trying to understand problems, fix ideas, and explore new directions helped me grow both scientifically and humanly.
Xavi, Laurent, and Chris will remain models of dedication to me.

Besides my great supervisors, I had the honor of working with inspiring collaborators.
The RobotLearn team brings together young, talented, and driven individuals from diverse cultures, backgrounds, and experiences to tackle challenging research projects.
It was always a blast to exchange ideas about highly specialized and novel subjects with curious and brilliant minds.
Experiencing the rapid progress of AI over these past five years together was a deeply immersive and stimulating adventure.
Our reading group sessions offered great opportunities to dive into challenging, cutting-edge topics.
Everyone was encouraged to ask questions and share their views, creating a supportive and enriching atmosphere.
I was grateful to share my successes, failures, and doubts with my teammates, who were always keen to offer their support.
Some of my fondest memories come from our daily meals at the "Champ de l'Étoile", enjoying Patrick's desserts, our coffee breaks, and many excursions.

Xiaoyu Lin started her PhD at the same time as I did.
I have hardly known someone as exceptionally hard-working and dedicated.
I have the utmost respect for her discretion, kindness and maturity.
She will undoubtedly have a successful and inspiring career that I will follow closely.
Andres, Louis, Alex, Anand, Kiru, Victor, and Lorenzo quickly became close friends, consistently cheering me up and making every shared moment enjoyable.
Radu, Soraya and Nicolas represent the roots and enduring spirit of the team, and hearing from their long-standing experience in research was always a pleasure.
I would also like to warmly thank the many other members of RobotLearn I had the chance to meet during these years, including Samir, Ahamed, Stéphane, Matthieu, Tim, Luis, Guillaume, Yihong, Xiaoyu Bie, Wen, David, Ghazi, Zhiqi, Daniel, Natanaël, Alexandre and Saghar.
One must not forget Nathalie, our team assistant, without whom this bunch of nerds would definitely not get very far!

Now, let's travel back in time.
My academic path did not begin with this PhD, and if I were able to reach the level required to join such a talented team, it is thanks to the excellent professors I had the chance to meet and the diverse academic environments I was fortunate to experience.
My years in the _La Martinière Monplaisir classes préparatoires_ helped me build solid and rigorous scientific foundations.
There, I discovered the beauty of mathematics, physics and engineering with exceptionally dedicated professors such as Viviane Gaggioli, Laurence Lechuga, Cédric Gamelon, Xavier Pessoles, and Delphine Sembély.
Their high expectations taught me the pursuit of scientific rigor and hard work.
My time at _Ensimag_ then opened my eyes to the fascinating world of computer science, mathematics and their application to the mysterious field of artificial intelligence.
I met countless like-minded students, eager to explore intricate topics and share unforgettable moments.
Looking back, I am profoundly grateful for the ten fulfilling years I have spent in outstanding academic environments, culminating in this PhD.

I am grateful for the fantastic friends with whom I shared so many warm and carefree moments.
Our dinners, long discussions, hikes, and board game sessions were always a wonderful way to escape the daily routine.
Lucas, Isabelle, Benjamin and Thomas Girerd in Lyon, as well as Olivier Lim, Thomas Bauvent and Michael from Grenoble — thank you for all these moments.
Last but not least, my fellow flatmates Antoine, Olivier Brun, and Yangtao shared the PhD journey with me day to day.
Living with these cheerful guys and sharing our victories, and doubts made this period lighter and more enjoyable.

I have practiced rock climbing for many years, and Grenoble has offered an exceptional environment to grow and progress in this sport.
Being able to enjoy this passion was crucial to my well-being.
Beyond the well-known physical and mental benefits of climbing, I want to emphasize how important its social dimension has been for me.
Climbing allowed me to disconnect from the computer screen, experience profound moments, and surround myself with wonderful people.
The climbing community in Grenoble is full of talented and welcoming climbers who are willing to share and teach their passion.
I had the pleasure of meeting numerous partners during the past 5 years.
Rémy, Marjorie, Simon, Basile, Nicolas, Lionel, Thomas, Hugo, Gabin, Noé, Lilou, Coraline, Thomas, Merlin, Manu and all the other _Requins du CSU_ were incredible training and traveling partners.
Our climbing trips to Chamonix, Fontainebleau, Céüse and especially Ailefroide are memories I will never forget.
The more experienced _adeptes de la force droite_ Nico, Théo, Roman and Mathieu have been strong, dedicated, and kind training companions whom I have always looked up to.
I also owe a lot to my coach, Adrien Pirolo who supported me throughout the past years.
Thanks to his knowledge, understanding and kindness, I have been able to push myself far harder than I could have imagined.
His trust in my potential and his valuable advice helped me tremendously in my progression.
I would not have dared to try the projects he helped me ascend.
Let's say that he was my fourth supervisor!

// == Family
My parents, Anne-Catherine and Francis, as well as my brother Tanguy, have provided me with unconditional and loving support.
They were always by my side during the difficult periods of this adventure, reminding me that life is not only about academic success, intricate programs and complex equations.
I was exceptionally lucky to have them around, and I truly realized how crucial and fundamental a loving family is.
They deserve a large share of this success, as I would probably have given up without them.

I would like to express my sincere gratitude to the jury members, Prof. Didier Schwab, Prof. Elisa Ricci, Prof. Patrick Danès and Dr. Romain Serizel, who agreed to review my work and participate in my defense.
I am honored to benefit from their expertise and their perspective on my work.
Patrick and Didier went through a very careful review of my manuscript and gave me thoughtful and precise feedback.

Last but not least, thank you to all the people who attended my defense.
I was delighted to be surrounded by so many friendly faces on such an important day.
Sharing this success with all of them was the best celebration I could have hoped for.
